Inteligeo decision 18 (2026-09-22): the documents API no longer reads a path or a
URL named by the client (local file read and server-side request forgery).

Target: GeoNode 4.3.1 as installed by this image (site-packages/geonode). Applied
with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` from site-packages (paths are geonode/...).

No advisory and no fix commit: found in the review of the 5.5.4 update. GeoNode
5.0 does not have the field any more (removed in the upload rewrite, PR #14223,
2026-05-14), so there is nothing to transpose; this patch is Inteligeo's own.

What happened: POST /api/v2/documents/ accepted a write-only string field
`file_path` (documents/api/serializers.py) and, in perform_create
(documents/api/views.py), handed it to StorageManager(remote_files=...), whose
data retriever opens the string with smart_open: a filesystem path of the
container or an http(s) URL. The copy became a document the caller can download.
`doc_file`, the multipart upload the clients use, went through the same line and
accepted a string too (`file if isinstance(file, str) else file.name`). The route
needs only a logged-in user with add_resourcebase, which every registered user has.
Measured 2026-09-22 in instancia_r, before the patch: `-F file_path=/etc/hostname`
-> 201 and the download returned the container's hostname; the same with
`-F doc_file=/etc/hostname` and with JSON {"doc_file": "/etc/hostname"};
`-F file_path=http://127.0.0.1:8001/static/geonode/img/logo.png` -> 201 with a GET
from 127.0.0.1 in the access log.

The change: the `file_path` field and its DynamicComputedField subclass are gone
from the serializer; the view accepts `doc_file` only when it has a read()
(an uploaded file) and answers 400 "doc_file must be an uploaded file" to a
string; `doc_url` is untouched (it goes through is_safe_url since
CVE-2026-39922 and the thumbnail no longer fetches it since CVE-2026-39921). The
docstring's JSON example that showed a server path is replaced by the form-data
example. Nothing in the Inteligeo repositories sends `file_path` (grep in
inteligeo-mapstore, inteligeo-next, inteligeo-api, inteligeo-geonode,
inteligeo-dados, qgis-configuracao, 2026-09-22); the MapStore client uploads
`doc_file` as multipart.

Files touched: geonode/documents/api/serializers.py, geonode/documents/api/views.py.
Neither is among the 13 files inteligeo-geonode overrides (its Dockerfile, lines
48-76). Applied on a clean copy of the installed package with
`patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --no-backup-if-mismatch`: 2 files, 0 FAILED, 0 fuzz;
`python -m py_compile` clean on both.

